MassDB OSS defaults on top of Apache Cassandra 5.0.8 conf/jvm17-server.options, applied with
patch -p1 -F0 by package/build/massdb-meta-package.sh (see package/README.md).

--- a/conf/jvm17-server.options
+++ b/conf/jvm17-server.options
@@ -120,3 +120,10 @@
 -Dio.netty.allocator.maxOrder=11
 
 # The newline in the end of file is intentional
+
+### MassDB OSS: heap size
+# The platform renders -Xms and -Xmx here, as a pair, from the host's memory
+# (a quarter of it, below 31G so compressed oops stay on). Without them
+# cassandra-env.sh computes the heap itself.
+#-Xms8G
+#-Xmx8G
